    "rootCause": "Outer native API write transaction retained a prefetch row lock after application-lock release; concurrent receipt GET inverted lock order.",
    "fix": "Native Catalog-launch, resource-change and upgrade action operands use only exact framework request markers and authorized read snapshots. No prefetch observation writes or retained plan/credential row locks precede the action application lock. Ordinary GET observation and final action owner, role, Key revision, source/snapshot, CAS and one-claim checks remain; no timeout, retry, schema or grant expansion. New upgrade plans bind the complete strategy in their private target snapshot so older engines reject them before claim; genuine legacy image-only plans keep classic snapshots and original defaults.",
